[38;5;252m[1m## What was found and fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The translation was already functionally complete for happy paths — symbol parity was empty from the start. Three real fidelity defects surfaced:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m1. Missing [38;5;10massert()[0m semantics (the big one).[22m [38;5;10mc_src/CMakeLists.txt[0m sets no [38;5;10mCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE[0m and never defines [38;5;10mNDEBUG[0m, so the reference [38;5;10m.so[0m imports [38;5;10m__assert_fail[0m — a failed assertion [38;5;10mabort()[0ms. The Rust had deliberately elided all nine asserts as no-ops, so on malformed input C died and Rust returned a value. I translated all nine literally under a new default-on [38;5;10mc_asserts[0m feature; with [38;5;10mpanic = "abort"[0m the Rust now aborts on exactly the same inputs. [38;5;10m--no-default-features[0m gives [38;5;10m-DNDEBUG[0m semantics, and [38;5;10mrun_all.sh[0m builds a second C library with [38;5;10m-DNDEBUG[0m (out-of-source, [38;5;10mc_src/[0m untouched) so each Rust combination has a matching reference.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m2. [38;5;10mcp_build[0m faulted where C survives.[22m [38;5;10mcounts[lens[n]]++[0m indexes an [38;5;10mint[16][0m with a value up to 255 when a malformed dynamic block or mutated [38;5;10mcp_fixed_table[0m yields a code length ≥ 16. C does an out-of-bounds stack write; Rust hit an array bounds check and aborted on inputs C keeps running past. Widened the three arrays to 256 entries.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m3. [38;5;10mcode << (32 - len)[0m[22m can shift by ≥ 32 with a corrupt tree entry. Switched to [38;5;10mwrapping_shl[0m/[38;5;10mwrapping_shr[0m to match the masking the compiled C actually performs.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Test surface[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mSYMBOLS.md[0m (9 ABI symbols, diff empty), [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m (11 error rows, 9 assert rows, 6 UB rows, 4 dead-code rows), [38;5;10mCONFIGS.md[0m (40 configuration rows) — all derived from the C source. Roughly 4,000 lines of tests, all going through [38;5;10mdlopen[0m/[38;5;10mdlsym[0m on both [38;5;10m.so[0ms. Includes a purpose-built DEFLATE encoder so I could drive stored/fixed/dynamic blocks, every length- and distance-extra-bit width, code-length symbols 16/17/18, and both sides of [38;5;10mcp_build[0m's 9-bit lookup cutoff; a 1,150-record zlib corpus; and a child-process harness that compares exit status so abort-vs-abort is checked precisely rather than "both failed".[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Things worth knowing[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two C behaviours turned out to be genuinely undefined and are documented rather than asserted on: [38;5;10mcp_dynamic[0m's repeat codes can overshoot its 320-byte stack array and smash its own frame (C spins until killed), and [38;5;10mcp_build[0m with a length ≥ 16 corrupts its frame once [38;5;10mNDEBUG[0m removes the guarding assert. The affected fuzz tests are scoped to avoid those paths, with one [38;5;10m#[ignore][0md test left in place explaining why.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Separately, my reference model was wrong twice, not the Rust: a stored block is only ever accepted as the [3mlast[23m thing in a stream ([38;5;10mbits_left / 8 <= LEN[0m), and [38;5;10mcp_ptr()[0m recovers the stored payload from the input buffer, so a payload sitting in the final partial word is copied as zeros (12 of 1,150 zlib records). Both are faithfully reproduced.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Run everything with [38;5;10mcd translation && ./run_all.sh[0m (~6 min, dominated by the abort-differential child processes).[0m[0m
